There is no cost data for pool-01-401 in that period, so I cannot give finance a figure for GUID rc9jt.

To be precise about what came back rather than what did not: the Azure query for 2026-05-01 to 2026-05-31 did return data -- one subscription, pool-01-402, at $310 -- so the tool worked and the period is queryable. pool-01-401 simply has no row in the result.

I am not going to render that as $0. An absent row and a measured zero are different things, and finance would act on them differently.

What could account for it, in the order I would check:

- the subscription may be right but have had no billable resources in May, in which case Azure emits no rows rather than zero-valued ones;
- the sandbox may have been provisioned outside this period, so its charges sit in a different month;
- the GUID-to-subscription mapping may be wrong or mistyped -- pool-01-402 is one digit away and did return data, which is worth ruling out first;
- the result came from the cache, refreshed 2026-06-01, so a subscription added after that refresh would not appear yet.

Confirming which of those it is means checking the sandbox account record for the real subscription name before anyone reports a number.
